SDE compositor: reload the configuration in place.

SDE 0.2.0 Alpha 3.1 (docs/THEMES.md, "Switching themes"). SDE reloads the
compositor whenever the theme, the accent or the transparency changes:
sde-session sends SIGUSR1 when the generated configuration changes, and
picom also watches the file. Upstream picom answers both with a full reset:
it unredirects every window, closes the X connection, connects again and
starts the backend again. On every theme change the screen then showed
windows without compositing for a frame (the panel blank, translucent
windows without their alpha) or, with OpenGL, froze for as long as the
backend took to start (2.8 seconds with Mesa's software OpenGL on Xvfb,
twice per switch in SDE 0.2.0 Alpha 3).

With this patch SIGUSR1 and changes of the configuration file reload the
configuration in place, a moment later (30 ms, so the signal and the file
watch, and the files SDE writes in a row, give one reload):

* the file is parsed again with the same command line; an unreadable file
  keeps the running configuration (a file being edited by hand);
* an unchanged file and unchanged shader files reload nothing: a file
  written again with the same text does nothing, and SIGUSR1 (which
  scripts, and SDE's screenshot tool after a resize with software
  OpenGL, send to have the screen drawn again: upstream's reset did
  that) gives every mapped window its image and rules again and
  repaints the whole screen once, still without a reset;
* options that the running backend cannot follow (the backend, vsync,
  damage, frame pacing, unredirection, D-Bus, logging, the detection
  options, the fading options that the running animations were generated
  from, custom animations and "rules") still reset the session as before;
* otherwise the windows, the redirection and the backend stay. The new
  options take the place of the old ones (their lists are moved with
  them), the window conditions get a new state and every window its
  properties again, the shaders are loaded again (a compiled shader whose
  source did not change is kept), the blur context and the shadow renderer
  are made again only when their settings changed (compiling them is slow
  with software OpenGL), every mapped window gets its rules, opacity,
  shadow and rounded-corner mask again (as after a resize, the window
  keeping its size), and the layout history starts afresh so that the
  next frame repaints the whole screen once (picom 12 repaints what its
  layout history says changed: after a new shadow renderer, whose back
  image starts empty, the rest of the screen stayed black);
* the file watch is set up again: SDE replaces the file, which ends the
  watch of the old one.

"Configuration reloaded in place." is logged at the info level.

